# Citation metadata for PEEL-Local (Citation File Format 1.2.0).
# https://citation-file-format.github.io
#
# TO FILL IN BEFORE PUBLICATION: `preferred-citation` has no journal, volume,
# or DOI yet, because the paper is still in pre-submission revision. Add them
# at acceptance, together with each author's ORCID, and bump `version` and
# `date-released` if a later tag supersedes v1.0.0-paper.

cff-version: 1.2.0
message: >-
  If you use PEEL-Local, please cite the paper below rather than only the
  software. If you reproduce or build on a specific run's artifacts, also
  cite the software version whose tag produced them.
title: PEEL-Local
abstract: >-
  A modular, auditable architecture for researcher-governed AI-assisted text
  summarization. Runs a four-phase local pipeline -- corpus cleaning; WordNet
  and GlossBERT word-sense disambiguation with sentence-transformer/HDBSCAN
  semantic clustering; lexical-density sentence selection with locally-hosted
  LLM condensation and independent adversarial review; and self-contained
  distant-reading analysis -- in which every interpretive decision is both an
  interactive prompt and a logged, timestamped audit record.
type: software
license: Apache-2.0
repository-code: https://github.com/PUC-Behring-AI/peel-local
version: 1.0.0-paper
date-released: 2026-09-15
keywords:
  - AI-assisted summarization
  - epistemic control
  - human-in-the-loop
  - natural language processing
  - word sense disambiguation
  - distant reading

